<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Unchanged core (Thompson's own Fig. 405 net as an exact-interpolation TPS, affine + bending decomposition, Lean-checked laws) plus the lambda sweep that now demonstrates the affine limit numerically (bending 2.10 -> 0.49 at lambda 10 with the affine-only end point at -0.12). The k* scan recovers Thompson's \"increased intensity\" ordering (0.85 < 1.15 < 1.30) from the real specimens. Remaining deduction: Figs. 407-408 nets still not digitised, so the baboon and dog transformations Thompson actually drew are not reconstructed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/scout_manifest.json L1–L40: Fig. 407/408 nets not digitised <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a5007b9c0/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/scout_manifest.json#L1-L40>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-058-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Cartesian transformation of the human skull into chimpanzee, baboon and dog (Figs. 404-408) — Morphometric validation: 70/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every headline now has an uncertainty and a null: jitter bootstrap CIs on E, the orderings (P = 1.00 for d_HC < d_HB < d_HD, 0.998 / 0.94 for the facial index / angle orderings), permutation p = 0.0005, r / RMSE / KS / Wilcoxon on per-landmark residuals, mirrored-net and specificity controls, and image-segmentation morphometrics independent of the landmarks (taper, face fraction). Facial angles sit inside the Camper bands. Deductions: n = 11 landmarks makes the KS test low-powered (p 0.075); no published landmark table for these exact taxa was found, so the only literature anchors are the Camper bands; one specimen per taxon means the bootstrap covers digitisation error, not biological variation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5.1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/t1917_058_metrics.json (generated output, not in repo): pass2.goodness_of_fit.ks_pvalue 0.075 (n=11, low power) — datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-058/t1917_058_metrics.json: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-058_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py at a5007b9c0, application/json, 49339 B, artifact_sha256 e96b962e952b3dbd3098ff99539074900d47c0f048b6b616b11c74631e90b09c (sha256 e96b962e952b3dbd3098ff99539074900d47c0f048b6b616b11c74631e90b09c), spec_fingerprint 974f3b1907dd69da0acb085b9f36dedce4c4532b025e0bf27519cd77a4567dc9" ;
